  itemName: Powder Horn
  itemIcon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 60317c2c8b6243841b0371b1fdd09292, type: 3}
  description: A Militia soldier needed two powder horns. The larger for containing
    the coarse powder for the main charge in the musket and the smaller to hold the
    more finely ground power that was used in the priming pan. These horns were made
    from real horns that were often obtained from domestic cattle.
